    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 71 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted every rejection response (400, 409, 429) to return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body while keeping the HTTP status codes unchanged.\n\n**What was there:** The escalation handlers for the `POST /api/owners` rule chain returned plain `{\"errors\":[...]}` JSON with `Content-Type: application/json`. A helper `ProblemDetails.build(...)` already existed and was used by the framework-level handlers (validation, forbidden, general, data-integrity).\n\n**What I changed** \u2014 the 12 rejection handlers in `src/main/java/.../rest/escalation/`:\n\n- **400 (Bad Request):** `OwnerFieldsMissing`, `OwnerEmailInvalid`, `OwnerEmailDisposable`, `OwnerPostcodeInvalid`, `OwnerRegistrationDateInvalid`, `OwnerTelephoneInvalid`, plus the existing `Validation` handler.\n- **409 (Conflict):** `OwnerCityCapacityExceeded`, `OwnerEmailDuplicate`, `OwnerHouseholdDuplicate`, `OwnerIdentityDuplicate`, `OwnerTelephoneDuplicate`.\n- **429 (Too Many Requests):** `OwnerDailyLimitExceeded`.\n\nEach now builds a `ProblemDetail` via `ProblemDetails.build(ex, status, ex.getMessage())` \u2014 populating the required `type`, `title`, `status` and `detail` members \u2014 and sends `ResponseEntity.status(status).contentType(MediaType.APPLICATION_PROBLEM_JSON).body(detail)`. I kept the original field name(s) as an `errors` extension member so the diagnostic detail isn't lost.\n\n**Key finding:** OfficeFloor's `ObjectResponse` does not infer `application/problem+json` from a `ProblemDetail` body (it defaulted to `application/json`), so I set the content type explicitly on the `ResponseEntity` \u2014 verified empirically against the new `Cp59Tests` before rolling it out to all handlers.\n\nThe `OwnerIdempotentReplay` (200) and `NotFound` (404) handlers were left untouched, as they aren't in-scope rejections.",
